    "body": "Evergreen Marine reported after-tax net profit of $2.16 billion for the first nine months of 2026, up 18.13% from a year earlier, as a strong third quarter boosted the Taiwanese container carrier’s earnings.\nThe world’s seventh-largest liner said consolidated revenue for January through September rose 15.36% to $10.29 billion. Earnings per share reached approximately $1.00, surpassing the approximately $0.96 recorded for all of 2025.\nThe Taiwan company’s ( 2603.TW ) third-quarter after-tax net profit surged 114.36% year over year to $1.42 billion, while consolidated revenue increased 51.44% to $4.46 billion. Quarterly earnings per share reached approximately $.65, an eight-quarter high.\nThird-quarter profit increased by approximately $756.1 million from a year earlier. The quarterly net profit margin reached 31.76%, compared with 20.96% for the first nine months, reflecting stronger peak-season freight rates and improved load factors.\nContainer shipping demand that began strengthening in the second quarter continued into the third, sustaining peak-season momentum throughout the period.\nAt the same time, unresolved geopolitical disruptions and congestion at major global hub ports reduced effective shipping capacity. That tighter supply-demand balance supported higher revenue and profit, while stronger utilization of available vessel space helped improve margins.\nWhy it matters: Evergreen’s nine-month results demonstrate the earnings impact of a strong peak season: third-quarter profit more than doubled, helping the company exceed its full-year 2025 earnings per share in just nine months.\nRead more articles by Stuart Chirls here .\nRead more:\nWhite House to extend Jones Act waiver as deadline nears, sources say\nRecord October as Los Angeles tops 1 Million TEUs for second straight month\nHapag-Lloyd profit jumps as stronger freight rates drive guidance upgrade\nUS midterm shift adds trade uncertainty as trans-Pacific ocean freight rates stay elevated\nUS postpones ‘million-dollar’ China ship tax until January",
